"id": "future",
"el": "Ο μέλλοντας",
"title": "The future: θα and its uses",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "The two futures (θα γράψω \"I'll write\" and θα γράφω \"I'll be writing\"), how to form the dependent stem, the future in time clauses (όταν έρθεις, without θα), and θα for guesses: θα είναι κουρασμένος \"he must be tired\".",
"intro": [
{
"p": "The future is the easy tense: the particle **θα** plus a verb form you already know. **Θα γράψω** \"I'll write\" uses the **dependent form** (aorist stem + present endings). **Θα γράφω** \"I'll be writing / I'll write regularly\" uses the plain present. Θα never changes and nothing comes between it and the verb except weak pronouns: **θα το γράψω**."
},
